1
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:08,880
Welcome to the Build America Buy America Act training series.

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:14,880
Before continuing, please watch the other videos within our training series on FEMA's Buy America website

3
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,880
to ensure you have the essential background knowledge.

4
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:23,880
As the other training videos explain, the Build America Buy America Act mandates that federal agencies,

5
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:29,880
including FEMA, must ensure that all of the iron, steel, manufactured products,

6
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:34,880
and construction materials incorporated into the project funded by federal financial assistance

7
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,880
are made in the U.S.

8
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:41,880
But remember, FEMA's Disaster Financial Assistance Grants are exempt from these requirements.

9
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:46,880
The Build America Buy America Act applies to articles, materials,

10
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:51,880
and supplies that are consumed in, incorporated into, or affixed to an infrastructure project.

11
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:56,880
It does not apply to Section 70917C materials,

12
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:00,880
tools, equipment, and supplies that are brought to the construction site

13
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:03,880
and removed at or before the completion of the project,

14
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:09,880
or building equipment and furnishings, such as movable chairs, desks, or portable equipment.

15
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:13,880
The classification of a product is determined based on its status

16
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:18,880
at the time it is brought to the project site for incorporation into the project.

17
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:24,880
This video will discuss the categories of products subject to the Build America Buy America Act,

18
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:29,880
as well as one category that is exempt by law by answering these five questions.

19
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:34,880
What is considered an iron or steel product under the Build America Buy America Act?

20
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:39,880
What is considered a construction material under the Build America Buy America Act?

21
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:44,880
What is considered a manufactured product under the Build America Buy America Act?

22
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,880
What are Section 70917C materials?

23
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:52,880
Where can you find more information about the Build America Buy America Act?

24
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,880
Now, let's discuss the first question.

25
00:01:55,880 --> 00:02:00,880
What is considered an iron or steel product under the Build America Buy America Act?

26
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:06,880
Iron or steel products are articles, materials, or supplies that consist wholly or predominantly

27
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:09,880
of iron or steel or a combination of both.

28
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:13,880
A product is considered iron or steel if the cost of the iron and steel content

29
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:17,880
exceeds 50% of the total cost of all of its components.

30
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:21,880
For an iron and steel product to be compliant with the Build America Buy America Act,

31
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:25,880
all the iron and steel used in the product must have been made in the U.S.

32
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:29,880
and the final product must have been manufactured in the U.S.

33
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:33,880
from the initial melting stage through the application of coatings.

34
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:36,880
A few examples of iron and steel products include

35
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:43,880
plant posts, wire rods, manhole covers, pipes, and structural steel, such as rebar.

36
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:46,880
Now, let's move on to the next question.

37
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:51,880
What is considered a construction material under the Build America Buy America Act?

38
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:59,880
Construction materials are articles, materials, or supplies that consist of one or more of the following items.

39
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:09,880
Nonferrous metals, plastic and polymer-based products, glass, fiber optic cable, optical fiber, lumber, engineered wood, and drywall.

40
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:14,880
Minor additions of articles, materials, supplies, or binding agents

41
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:18,880
do not change the categorization of the product as a construction material.

42
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,880
Now, let's move on to the third question.

43
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:25,880
What is considered a manufactured product under the Build America Buy America Act?

44
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:33,880
Manufactured products are articles, materials, or supplies that have been processed into a specific form and shape,

45
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:42,880
or combined with other articles, materials, or supplies to create a product with different properties than the individual articles, materials, or supplies.

46
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:50,880
If a product is not primarily iron or steel or not listed as a construction material, it is likely a manufactured product.

47
00:03:50,880 --> 00:04:02,880
Examples of manufactured products include, but are not limited to, pumps, motors, transformers, generators, and instrumentation or control systems.

48
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:08,880
All manufactured products purchased with FEMA financial assistance must be produced in the US.

49
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:15,880
This means that the cost of the components of the manufactured product that are mined, produced, or manufactured in the US

50
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:20,880
must be greater than 55% of the total cost of all components that make up the product.

51
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:25,880
An example is a manufacturing facility in Missouri that produces generators.

52
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:29,880
The materials the facility uses account for 35% of the generator's cost.

53
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:33,880
Another 30% of the cost is incurred at a facility in Oregon,

54
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:38,880
and the remaining cost of the components is sourced from a facility outside the US.

55
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:44,880
Once complete, the generator is considered a Build America Buy America Act compliant product

56
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:48,880
because, in this specific case, the product was manufactured in the US

57
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:53,880
and over 55% of the cost of the components were produced in the US.

58
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:56,880
Next, we will discuss the fourth question.

59
00:04:56,880 --> 00:05:00,880
What are Section 70917C materials?

60
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:07,880
Section 70917C materials, named after the corresponding section of the Build America Buy America Act,

61
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:13,880
refer to a list of items which are specifically exempt by law from the domestic preference requirements.

62
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:20,880
These include cement and cementitious materials, aggregates such as stone, sand, or gravel,

63
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:24,880
and aggregate binding agents or additives.

64
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:27,880
Now, let's discuss the last question.

65
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:32,880
Where can I find more information on the Build America Buy America Act?

66
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:37,880
You can find information on FEMA's implementation of the Build America Buy America Act

67
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:42,880
on our website located under the Buy America Preference tab on FEMA.gov.

68
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:50,880
This website includes a list of all FEMA grant programs subject to and not subject to the Build America Buy America Act.

69
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:56,880
You can also find more program definitions, flyers, and a helpful decision roadmap.

70
00:05:56,880 --> 00:06:06,880
The Code of Federal Regulations website provides more information on the Build America Buy America Act policy under 2 CFR Part 184.

71
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:12,880
Thank you for watching this video on the Build America Buy America Act categories of products.

72
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:17,880
To continue learning, be sure to check out the other videos in this training series.

73
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:22,880
For more information, please visit FEMA's Buy America website on FEMA.gov

74
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:32,880
or contact us at FEMA-grants-buyamerica at FEMA.dhs.gov.

